diff --git a/docs/CHANGELOG.md b/docs/CHANGELOG.md
index 9636f54..3aed6c8 100644
--- a/docs/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/docs/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,23 @@ All notable changes to the Οργανική Ονοματολογία MuLERMoC.
 
 Forked from v54 (`mulermoc-nom-55.html` + `js/*-55.js` + `css/*-55.css`, `?v=55.0`). Draft 3D is now 3-tier: PubChem SDF → JSmol remote `load $SMILES` (`fMolDraftRemote3DFromJSmol`: applet proxy-routed, works CDN + local, no page-side fetch so no CORS wall; scriptWait + SDF read-back, validated) → local 2D-MOL + UFF minimize in JSmol (offline, `fMolDraftLocal3DFromMol`: inline `load data` + `add hydrogens` + blocking `minimize steps 500` via scriptWait — fire-and-forget raced read-back with pre-minimize coords — then SDF extracted back via `molFile`/`show MOL`, validated by `fMolDraftValidSDF3D` heavy-count + non-flat-z). Orchestrated by `fMolDraftFetchSDF3DTiered` with epoch/submitId guards; preview shows source-labeled 3D row (local flagged provisional), fetching note, all-miss 2D-only note. Accept ungated on any tier success (was PubChem-3D-only); provenance persisted as `sdf3DSource` (rec + update path + history + save-file headers). SDF read-back is `write MOL` alone (translate-test proved it the sole live-model serializer: `molFile` returns an unparseable layout, `fileContents` is a stale dump), logging length + heavy count + heavy-only z-spread + verdict. The V2000 parser now reads z (flat-2D text correctly fails the non-flat check, spread over heavies only so H-noise can't fake 3D). The planar-saddle trap (exactly-flat input freezes MMFF: zero heavy displacement) plus E=46000+ overlap divergence are broken by a pure-JS 2D untangle (spreads non-bonded heavy overlaps) + z-jiggle (±0.3 Å), both self-verifying, with tier-3 acceptance requiring heavy displacement vs the prepared input (`fMolDraftMovedEnough`, mean ≥ 0.05 Å) plus plain-`minimize` retry; `zap`-first loads with `calculate hydrogens`, live load-verify (heavy count + matches-loaded ≈ 0), always-show-flat-3D on total miss, and a manual Minimize-3D fallback button in the preview: pressing it runs the pipeline, then an OK-only dialog asks to save the 3D conformation once optimization completes — OK stores best-effort (`jsmol-min` when validated, `jsmol-unminimized` live model otherwise) and unlocks Accept (ESC/backdrop = back out, stay locked). Minimize is fire-and-forget (follow-up scripts interrupt the in-flight run — console-proven) with a single delayed read-back, explicit MMFF-then-UFF force fields, and iterative re-minimize from the live model on repeat presses (movement judged vs the pre-fire snapshot, no convergence requirement — partial descent counts). `?v=55.0` unchanged across all v55 commits — hard-reload (Ctrl+Shift+R) after pulling. No naming-engine changes.
 
+### Minimizing status + wait window (v55, post-handoff batch)
+- Auto tier-3 sets `#molDraftStatus` to `draftMinimizing` ("Ελαχιστοποίηση 3D σε εξέλιξη… / Minimizing 3D… please wait.") at local-phase entry and restores `Preview: ‹name›` (+ same/different hint) after the tier resolves; the manual path already had it.
+- Blocking wait window (`#molDraftMinWait`, same overlay skin as the scenario confirm): flat 3D shown first in the viewer, Cancel aborts via `_submitId` invalidation (stale continuation guard-fails silently), ESC dismisses, backdrop deliberately does NOT cancel; live `(Ns)` countdown from a page-side interval (zero applet traffic), cleared on every close path.
+- Wait budget scaled by system size (`fMolDraftMinWaitSecs`: 10 s base to 30 heavies, +1 s/heavy above, cap 120 s); the relax sleep, both window call sites, and the fire log share it, so countdown and read-back always agree.
+- `minimize STOP` on Cancel-abort, Draw, and draft teardown (conditional no-ops when idle). Prophylactic STOP at run entries was tried and reverted the same session: sending STOP to the idle applet breaks the following inline load (verify reads heavy=0 deterministically, direct-Prepare split test) — noted at both sites so it is not re-added.
+- Save dialog removed: manual runs store best-effort directly (`_storeBest`), no OK window; Accept itself is the author confirmation and provenance stays labeled (`draftMinDone` / `draftMinUnminDone` / neutral further-miss toasts unchanged in role). Dialog code + `#molDraftMinOK` CSS block + `draftMinSave3D` key deleted.
+- Step budget consts: `MOLMIN_STEPS` (fresh/auto rounds, gated on ≥ 0.05 Å mean heavy displacement) + `MOLMIN_FURTHER_STEPS = 100` (further rounds from the last minimized geometry, no displacement gate — any valid candidate banks; a miss keeps the previous geometry with the renamed `draftMinFurtherMiss` "no valid result" toast, never a convergence claim). Verdict logs carry numeric `disp=`; further rounds skip preparation and deterministically reload the stored SDF first (zap + inline load + echo verify with echo-length logging) instead of trusting live applet state.
+- Re-optimize entry: `draftMinMore` ("Ελαχιστοποίηση +100 / Minimize +100") button on `jsmol-min` previews; the manual guard admits fresh + unminimized-retry + further, still blocks PubChem/remote 3D.
+- Root-caused this batch from console: the minimize command had been blanked to `" "` by an uncommitted worktree edit (bit-identical 2557-char read-backs, `unmoved — rejected` on both forcefields, small molecule included) — restored to `select all; minimize steps N`. In-tree owner tuning kept as-is: steps currently 300, `spt/init-3.spt` sets a global `minimizationCriterion 0.01`, green `.viewerFullBtn` restyle.
+
+### Settings panel cleanup + i18n rebuild (v55 working tree)
+- `#customMolSetting` row removed (label + per-session download button + counter); the title-bar `#saveMolBtn` is the single save entry (`fMolDraftSaveAllCustom` untouched). `acceptKept` toast reworded to point at it. No dedicated CSS existed.
+- `#atomSymbolsCheck` moved back to `#controls3D` (after hydrogens), out of the settings panel; all handlers/sync are id-based, no JS logic touched. Bar label translates via the value-matched bar list.
+- Settings labels are now `data-lang`-keyed with one generic loop — the positional label↔key map is deleted (it had silently rotated EN labels from the autoLinearize row onward; each label now fetches its own key, which also fixes that shift). AutoLinearize id-block removed (covered by its key).
+- `MULER_VIEWER_SETTINGS` registry + `fSyncViewerSettingsUI()` in molview: one entry per global-backed row (chain-mode radio, atom-color checkbox+radios+disabled state, both height sliders). Panel-open and scenario-apply sync go through it (replacing scattered per-id blocks); DOM-truth checkboxes (drawing, auto-tidy, highlight ×2, bond-atoms) keep their direct capture/apply paths. No DOM rebuild — all existing bindings survive untouched. Tabs hook: group by row id later.
+- EN fixes found live: the new data-lang loop initially used `(root || document)` in a rootless function (ReferenceError swallowed → loop dead, panel stayed Greek) and wrote `firstChild` (indentation whitespace on multi-line labels) — now queries `document` and writes the first non-empty text node (span-safe for the bar checkbox). `atomSymbolsBar` key (`Σύμβολα ατόμων` / `Atom Symbols`) for the bar label; orphaned `atomSymbols3D` key retired.
+
